WEBVTT

1
00:00:46.041 --> 00:00:47.208
<b>In the previous verse,</b>

2
00:00:47.208 --> 00:00:49.666
<b>Lord Krishna gave his own example,</b>

3
00:00:49.666 --> 00:00:55.333
<b>stating that he has no duties left to</b>
<b>perform in all three worlds,</b>

4
00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:57.166
<b>nor does he desire anything,</b>

5
00:00:57.166 --> 00:01:05.041
<b>yet he diligently performs his duties.</b>

6
00:01:05.041 --> 00:01:08.083
<b>Now, in these two verses, </b>
<b>Lord Krishna</b>

7
00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:10.458
<b>is shedding light on the negative consequences</b>

8
00:01:10.458 --> 00:01:17.083
<b>sthat would occur if he were to neglect his duties.</b>

9
00:01:21.875 --> 00:01:25.458
<b>In these verses, Lord Krishna tells Arjuna,</b>

10
00:01:25.458 --> 00:01:26.791
<b>"O Partha!</b>

11
00:01:26.791 --> 00:01:30.416
<b>If I were to abandon my duties,</b>

12
00:01:30.416 --> 00:01:36.208
<b>all men would follow my example </b>
<b>and forsake their own responsibilities.</b>

13
00:01:36.208 --> 00:01:37.375
<b>Not only this,</b>

14
00:01:37.375 --> 00:01:42.791
<b>but by neglecting my obligations, </b>
<b>the entire world would fall into chaos.</b>

15
00:01:42.791 --> 00:01:46.000
<b>I would become the cause of such anarchy,</b>

16
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.541
<b>which would destroy the </b>
<b>peace of all living beings."</b>

17
00:01:49.541 --> 00:01:52.166
<b>We must understand Lord Krishna's point.</b>

18
00:01:52.166 --> 00:01:55.458
<b>In this current avatar, Lord Krishna is a Kshatriya,</b>

19
00:01:55.458 --> 00:01:58.375
<b>a ruler, a statesman,</b>

20
00:01:58.375 --> 00:02:04.291
<b>and it is the responsibility of a good statesman </b>
<b>to participate in the world's politics.</b>

21
00:02:04.291 --> 00:02:10.375
<b>Only then can they ensure </b>
<b>that capable people govern.</b>

22
00:02:10.375 --> 00:02:15.750
<b>This is necessary for the welfare and </b>
<b>proper guidance of the people.</b>

23
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.708
<b>And that is precisely what He is doing,</b>

24
00:02:17.708 --> 00:02:19.583
<b>supporting the Pandavas</b>

25
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:21.791
<b>and upholding righteousness.</b>

26
00:02:21.791 --> 00:02:26.208
<b>Lord Krishna has used the word "atandritaḥ" here.</b>

27
00:02:26.208 --> 00:02:29.833
<b>This word is derived from the word "tandra,"</b>

28
00:02:29.833 --> 00:02:33.666
<b>which means to sleep or slumber,</b>

29
00:02:33.666 --> 00:02:35.500
<b>and its opposite is</b>

30
00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.708
<b>"atandritaḥ,"</b>

31
00:02:36.708 --> 00:02:40.333
<b> meaning to stay awake, to be vigilant.</b>

32
00:02:40.333 --> 00:02:41.291
<b>Imagine</b>

33
00:02:41.291 --> 00:02:46.791
<b>if the driver of a vehicle full of </b>
<b>passengers begins to doze off,</b>

34
00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:48.083
<b>what will happen?</b>

35
00:02:48.083 --> 00:02:50.041
<b>In such a case, an accident is certain,</b>

36
00:02:50.041 --> 00:02:52.333
<b>and the lives of the passengers may be lost.</b>

37
00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:55.541
<b>For this reason, that vehicle </b>
<b>driver must remain alert,</b>

38
00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:58.000
<b>i.e., "atandritaḥ."</b>

39
00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.541
<b>And what about Lord Krishna?</b>

40
00:02:59.541 --> 00:03:00.500
<b>Think about it.</b>

41
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.791
<b>He is the driver of this entire universe.</b>

42
00:03:02.791 --> 00:03:05.125
<b>He must always be vigilant</b>

43
00:03:05.125 --> 00:03:07.791
<b>so that humanity suffers no harm</b>

44
00:03:07.791 --> 00:03:12.291
<b>and everyone reaches their </b>
<b>destined spiritual place safely.</b>

45
00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:13.791
<b>The higher the level,</b>

46
00:03:13.791 --> 00:03:15.708
<b>the greater the responsibility.</b>

47
00:03:15.708 --> 00:03:16.916
<b>Consider,</b>

48
00:03:16.916 --> 00:03:21.875
<b>if Krishna Himself does not fulfill His </b>
<b>duty to side with righteousness,</b>

49
00:03:21.875 --> 00:03:25.291
<b>how much more strength </b>
<b>will unrighteousness gain?</b>

50
00:03:25.291 --> 00:03:31.125
<b>All those who are fighting on the side of </b>
<b>righteousness and truth will be disheartened.</b>

51
00:03:31.125 --> 00:03:35.625
<b>For all of them, Lord Krishna </b>
<b>is fulfilling this responsibility.</b>

52
00:03:35.625 --> 00:03:37.166
<b>We must understand</b>

53
00:03:37.166 --> 00:03:40.125
<b>that when people do not follow their duties,</b>

54
00:03:40.125 --> 00:03:46.583
<b>they do not hesitate to move in an </b>
<b>unrighteous direction to fulfill their needs.</b>

55
00:03:46.583 --> 00:03:50.708
<b>The coming generations also </b>
<b>learn from their elders.</b>

56
00:03:50.708 --> 00:03:53.875
<b>In such a situation, if people start</b>
<b>forgetting their duties,</b>

57
00:03:53.875 --> 00:03:56.291
<b>leaning towards unrighteousness,</b>

58
00:03:56.291 --> 00:03:58.583
<b>and becoming absorbed in sensual pleasures,</b>

59
00:03:58.583 --> 00:04:02.375
<b>it will also negatively impact </b>
<b>the coming generations.</b>

60
00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:09.208
<b>Those generations will also be deprived of crucial </b>
<b>life values such as culture and devotion to duty.</b>

61
00:04:09.208 --> 00:04:12.625
<b>Forgetting duty and responsibility, such </b>
<b>generations will begin to consider only pleasure </b>

62
00:04:12.625 --> 00:04:16.625
<b>and enjoyment as their goal.</b>

63
00:04:16.625 --> 00:04:17.500
<b>Selfishness</b>

64
00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.583
<b>and looting will increase.</b>

65
00:04:19.583 --> 00:04:23.041
<b>The strong will not hesitate to exploit the weak,</b>

66
00:04:23.041 --> 00:04:24.916
<b>and the day is not far off</b>

67
00:04:24.916 --> 00:04:30.625
<b>when the purity of women will also be</b>
<b>insulted on the altar of this lust.</b>

68
00:04:30.625 --> 00:04:36.291
<b>As a result of this social downfall, </b>
<b>only degraded lineages will be born.</b>

69
00:04:36.291 --> 00:04:37.625
<b>In the first chapter,</b>

70
00:04:37.625 --> 00:04:41.000
<b>Arjuna's view was that if he fought the war</b>

71
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.125
<b>and the elders of the family</b>
<b>were killed by his hands,</b>

72
00:04:44.125 --> 00:04:48.583
<b>ultimately the culture would be destroyed, </b>
<b>and society would decline.</b>

73
00:04:48.583 --> 00:04:49.500
<b>But</b>

74
00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:54.125
<b>here, Lord Krishna is indirectly trying to explain</b>

75
00:04:54.125 --> 00:04:55.166
<b>that Arjuna,</b>

76
00:04:55.166 --> 00:05:00.375
<b>the destruction of culture will happen </b>
<b>when you run away from your duties.</b>

77
00:05:00.375 --> 00:05:02.791
<b>But if you fight this war,</b>

78
00:05:02.791 --> 00:05:04.875
<b>righteousness will be strengthened,</b>

79
00:05:04.875 --> 00:05:08.000
<b>and society will be saved from downfall.</b>

80
00:05:12.708 --> 00:05:14.250
<b>Your decisions</b>

81
00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.666
<b>and responsibilities affect not only you</b>

82
00:05:17.666 --> 00:05:21.833
<b>but also the world around you. </b>

83
00:05:21.833 --> 00:05:24.083
<b>Imagine</b>

84
00:05:24.083 --> 00:05:25.625
<b>what would happen</b>

85
00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:33.541
<b>if everyone abandoned their duties, </b>
<b>thinking they were insignificant.</b>

86
00:05:33.541 --> 00:05:40.041
<b>What if a doctor refused to practice medicine,</b>

87
00:05:40.041 --> 00:05:42.375
<b>saying their job was too difficult?</b>

88
00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:46.916
<b>What if a farmer stopped tilling their fields?</b>

89
00:05:46.916 --> 00:05:50.875
<b>We all depend on each other,</b>

90
00:05:50.875 --> 00:05:54.083
<b>and we must understand that</b>

91
00:05:54.083 --> 00:05:58.958
<b>just as many other people fulfill their </b>
<b>responsibilities for us,</b>

92
00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:04.500
<b>we too must contribute to </b>
<b>society through our actions.</b>

93
00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:08.750
<b>And this is not limited to life's conveniences;</b>

94
00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:13.000
<b>it also impacts relationships.</b>

95
00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.083
<b>Take the example of two friends.</b>

96
00:06:16.083 --> 00:06:23.708
<b>If one friend constantly</b>
<b>ignores their commitments, </b>

97
00:06:23.708 --> 00:06:25.375
<b>never arrives on time,</b>

98
00:06:25.375 --> 00:06:27.291
<b>never checks in,</b>

99
00:06:27.291 --> 00:06:29.916
<b>and never helps,</b>

100
00:06:29.916 --> 00:06:35.166
<b>can such a one-sided relationship survive?</b>

101
00:06:35.166 --> 00:06:36.791
<b>No, right?</b>

102
00:06:36.791 --> 00:06:42.041
<b>In such a case, the entire burden of the</b>
<b>relationship will fall on only one friend,</b>

103
00:06:42.041 --> 00:06:44.666
<b>and eventually,</b>

104
00:06:44.666 --> 00:06:49.083
<b>even they will tire of carrying this load.</b>

105
00:06:49.083 --> 00:06:53.666
<b>Whether social responsibilities </b>
<b>or commitments in relationships,</b>

106
00:06:53.666 --> 00:06:58.041
<b>if a person begins to forget </b>
<b>the importance of their duties,</b>

107
00:06:58.041 --> 00:07:02.958
<b>the end can never be pleasant.</b>

108
00:07:02.958 --> 00:07:08.208
<b>Do not underestimate the importance </b>
<b>of yourself and your duties.</b>

109
00:07:08.208 --> 00:07:12.666
<b>Everyone is contributing to </b>
<b>society in their own way,</b>

110
00:07:12.666 --> 00:07:19.166
<b>so thinking of running away from </b>
<b>responsibilities is utterly inappropriate.</b>

111
00:07:23.791 --> 00:07:25.541
<b>Sometimes,</b>

112
00:07:25.541 --> 00:07:28.625
<b>the thought may cross your mind,</b>

113
00:07:28.625 --> 00:07:32.958
<b>"What is the benefit, what is </b>
<b>the importance of these duties?"</b>

114
00:07:32.958 --> 00:07:35.958
<b>You may feel like abandoning </b>
<b>these responsibilities.</b>

115
00:07:35.958 --> 00:07:40.916
<b>Why not just relax and enjoy?</b>

116
00:07:40.916 --> 00:07:42.625
<b>In such thoughts,</b>

117
00:07:42.625 --> 00:07:45.291
<b> we forget that</b>

118
00:07:45.291 --> 00:07:47.916
<b>the impact of our every action, big or small,</b>

119
00:07:47.916 --> 00:07:50.250
<b>is not limited to us</b>

120
00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:54.750
<b>but also leaves an impression on others.</b>

121
00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:58.291
<b>Take a typical family situation.</b>

122
00:07:58.291 --> 00:08:00.125
<b>Imagine</b>

123
00:08:00.125 --> 00:08:03.166
<b>what would happen if parents</b>

124
00:08:03.166 --> 00:08:07.375
<b>started prioritizing their comfort and enjoyment</b>

125
00:08:07.375 --> 00:08:17.208
<b>and, in doing so, neglected their responsibilities </b>
<b>towards their children and family.</b>

126
00:08:17.208 --> 00:08:20.208
<b>What happens then?</b>

127
00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:23.666
<b>Not every action is done solely for profit.</b>

128
00:08:23.666 --> 00:08:28.750
<b>Also, know that every action is important;</b>

129
00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:34.625
<b>you just have to look at </b>
<b>it from the right perspective.</b>

130
00:08:34.625 --> 00:08:40.958
<b>Neglecting family responsibilities </b>
<b>can have serious consequences. </b>

131
00:08:40.958 --> 00:08:44.708
<b>It can increase distances between people,</b>

132
00:08:44.708 --> 00:08:46.916
<b>create misunderstandings,</b>

133
00:08:46.916 --> 00:08:50.208
<b>and upset the family balance.</b>

134
00:08:50.208 --> 00:08:55.333
<b>Whether you fulfill a duty or abandon it,</b>

135
00:08:55.333 --> 00:09:00.375
<b>it will have an impact in both situations,</b>

136
00:09:00.375 --> 00:09:04.791
<b>especially on your closest relationships.</b>

137
00:09:04.791 --> 00:09:10.541
<b>Now, whether this impact will be positive </b>
<b>or negative is your choice.</b>

138
00:09:10.541 --> 00:09:11.875
<b>Think about it.</b>

139
00:09:11.875 --> 00:09:13.125
<b>What will you choose?</b>

140
00:09:13.125 --> 00:09:15.416
<b>To abandon family duties?</b>

141
00:09:15.416 --> 00:09:18.375
<b>Or to uphold them?</b>

142
00:09:22.791 --> 00:09:25.500
<b>In a professional context,</b>

143
00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:30.750
<b>it is crucial to fully understand </b>
<b>your responsibilities,</b>

144
00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:34.333
<b>especially when you are in a position</b>

145
00:09:34.333 --> 00:09:41.083
<b>where you are responsible for managing </b>
<b>and guiding some of your colleagues.</b>

146
00:09:41.083 --> 00:09:42.750
<b>For example,</b>

147
00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:47.625
<b>imagine that among the</b>
<b>colleagues who work with you,</b>

148
00:09:47.625 --> 00:09:53.583
<b>some are skilled at their jobs, while others are not.</b>

149
00:09:53.583 --> 00:09:59.708
<b>Your goals are met based on </b>
<b>those who are proficient. </b>

150
00:09:59.708 --> 00:10:03.916
<b>In such a situation, if you start thinking,</b>

151
00:10:03.916 --> 00:10:11.250
<b>"What is the benefit of helping those </b>
<b>who are not skilled in their work,</b>

152
00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:16.708
<b>because your work is going well anyway, </b>
<b>relying on others?"</b>

153
00:10:16.708 --> 00:10:25.041
<b>If you ignore your duty towards those people, </b>
<b>thinking this way,</b>

154
00:10:25.041 --> 00:10:27.208
<b>what will happen?</b>

155
00:10:27.208 --> 00:10:33.666
<b>What if one of the skilled members </b>
<b>of your team resigns,</b>

156
00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:40.750
<b>falls ill, or your workload increases?</b>

157
00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:44.083
<b>In such a situation, you will surely regret</b>

158
00:10:44.083 --> 00:10:54.750
<b>not guiding everyone and </b>
<b>monitoring everyone's progress.</b>

159
00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:59.416
<b>The impact of neglecting </b>
<b>responsibilities affects others,</b>

160
00:10:59.416 --> 00:11:05.458
<b>but ultimately it will also adversely affect you.</b>

161
00:11:05.458 --> 00:11:09.500
<b>Your colleagues also learn from you.</b>

162
00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:14.791
<b>If you start shirking your duties,</b>

163
00:11:14.791 --> 00:11:19.666
<b>don't you think this tendency </b>
<b>will spread to others as well?</b>

164
00:11:19.666 --> 00:11:24.833
<b>This will harm not only you </b>
<b>but also the organization.</b>

165
00:11:24.833 --> 00:11:27.041
<b>Be dutiful,</b>

166
00:11:27.041 --> 00:11:32.000
<b>no matter how small a </b>
<b>responsibility may be, fulfill it well.</b>

167
00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:36.583
<b>This is the path to progress in professional life.</b>

